                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "A client with testicular cancer is receiving cisplatin. The nurse assesses for which finding as a toxic effect of this medication?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nCisplatin is a medication that kills cells primarily by forming cross-links between and within strands of deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA). Its principal use is in the treatment of testicular cancer, although it also can be used to treat carcinomas of the ovary, bladder, head, and neck. It can cause neurotoxicity, nephrotoxicity, bone marrow depression, and ototoxicity, which manifests as tinnitus and high-frequency hearing loss. Nausea and vomiting are expected side effects, which can be severe and begin 1 hour after administration, persisting for 1 to 2 days. Diarrhea is not an associated side effect or toxic effect.",
                        "id": "36adcae361224709bfa95fc39663d5ea",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    }
